                <pb facs="0256" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/470.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Zenón Torribio is reported to have landed in the Dominican Republic via Haiti
                    with a revolutionary force of Dominicans and Haitians, and to be receiving aid
                    from the Haitian authorities. A Dominican gunboat has been dispatched to Dajabón
                    with a strong force. Torribio was one of the Morales group and is the only one
                    who escaped capture or death at San Juan last spring.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
